{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WritingAVendorDestination"],"title":"Guides","anchor":"Guides"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests"],"title":"Choosing what to record","anchor":"Choosing-what-to-record"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues","doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums"],"title":"Modules","anchor":"Modules"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting"],"title":"Testing","anchor":"Testing"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"Traffluent","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"Traffluent"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event is a struct, so the compiler checks its name and every property. A tracker holds back"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the events the user hasn’t consented to, stamps the rest with their session and device, keeps them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on disk and delivers them to your server, sending again when the network or the server fails."}]},{"anchor":"An-apps-analytics-from-launch","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"An app’s analytics, from launch"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare the events. The tracker rejects an event that breaks a constraint before it is stored or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered, and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value reaches only the destinations that don’t redact it:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import SwiftUI","import Traffluent","import TrackingPlans","","@Event(name: \"product_added_to_cart\")","struct ProductAddedToCart {","    var productID: String","    @Constrained(.minimum(1), .maximum(10))","    var quantity: Int","}","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","    var email: Sensitive<String>","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Build the tracker and start its delivery once, as the app launches:"}]},{"code":["func startAnalytics(consent: Consent) throws -> Tracker {","    \/\/ The plan and the store each take every @Event in the app, and the library's own.","    let plan = try TrackingPlan()","    \/\/ Records wait on disk until they are delivered, across launches.","    let store = try SegmentStore()","    \/\/ Every event gets its session, and the app, device, OS, locale and network it was tracked on.","    let tracker = Tracker(","        store: store,","        consent: consent,","        enrichers: [.sessions(), .application(), .device(), .operatingSystem(), .locale(), .network()])","","    let collector = HTTPDestination(","        endpoint: collectorURL,","        headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(apiKey)\"],","        encoder: CollectorBatchEncoder(plan: plan))","    \/\/ Analytics events only, without their email addresses, 20 at a time or every 30 seconds.","    let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(","        to: collector.accepting(.analytics).redactingSensitiveValues())","    Task {","        do {","            try await delivery.execute()  \/\/ for the life of the app","        } catch {","            print(\"Delivery stopped: \\(error)\")","        }","    }","","    \/\/ Every event that won't arrive, and why.","    let rejections = tracker.rejectionReports","    let consentDrops = consent.dropReports","    let storeDrops = store.dropReports","    let collectorDrops = collector.dropReports","    Task {","        await withDiscardingTaskGroup { group in","            group.addTask { for await report in rejections { print(\"Rejected: \\(report)\") } }","            group.addTask { for await report in consentDrops { print(\"Not consented: \\(report)\") } }","            group.addTask { for await report in storeDrops { print(\"Not stored: \\(report)\") } }","            group.addTask { for await report in collectorDrops { print(\"Not sent: \\(report)\") } }","        }","    }","    return tracker","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Then make the tracker the app’s default and hand it to the views, which track through it:"}]},{"code":["@main","struct StoreApp: App {","    let tracker: Tracker","","    init() {","        do {","            \/\/ The user's earlier decisions, which the app saved; undecided categories wait in memory.","            let tracker = try startAnalytics(consent: Consent(savedDecisions))","            \/\/ `Tracker.current` falls back to it where nothing else reaches, such as a detached task.","            try Tracker.bootstrap(tracker)","            self.tracker = tracker","        } catch {","            print(\"Analytics are off: \\(error)\")","            tracker = .noOp","        }","    }","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            CartView()","                .tracker(tracker)","        }","    }","}","","struct CartView: View {","    @Environment(\\.tracker) private var tracker","","    var body: some View {","        Button(\"Add to Cart\") {","            tracker.track(ProductAddedToCart(productID: \"canvas-tote\", quantity: 1))","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" imports every module except "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and the testing modules, which are products of their own."}]},{"anchor":"Where-to-go-next","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Where to go next"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Set it up step by step, from adding the package to testing what you track: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/GettingStarted"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare events and their constraints: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"; change one that has shipped:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Track from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit views: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews"},{"type":"text","text":"; let screens, controls and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the app’s lifecycle track themselves: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach the tracker from any code, batch records and add context to them: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep events when the app ends or goes offline before delivering them: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ask for consent and gate events by it: "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep a fraction of events or sessions: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Group events into sessions and stamp them with the app and device: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A session’s key is a UUIDv7, its start time in Unix milliseconds followed by random bits, held in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"memory only."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Export the events’ schemas and catch breaking changes in CI: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Test what your code tracks: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Send to logs, traces, your own server, PostHog or memory, with values for one destination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alone: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Send to an analytics vendor not yet covered, from a module of your own: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WritingAVendorDestination","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decide what belongs in an event and what stays out of it: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Typed analytics events for Swift, delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","type":"topic","title":"Traffluent","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Typed analytics events for Swift, delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"role":"collection"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","title":"Persistence","url":"\/documentation\/persistence","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TestingWhatYouTrack":{"type":"topic","title":"Testing What Your Code Tracks","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","title":"Defining Events","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","title":"Consent Gating","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","title":"Persisting Records","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending."}],"role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChangingEvents":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","type":"topic","title":"Changing an Event","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An event’s version counts the changes that records stored before them can’t be read through, and only those. A compatible change keeps the version; a breaking one raises it."}],"role":"article"},"doc://StandardContext/documentation/StandardContext":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","title":"StandardContext","url":"\/documentation\/standardcontext","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Stamp every event with the app, device, operating system, locale and network connection it was tracked on.","type":"text"}]},"doc://CollectorEncoding/documentation/CollectorEncoding":{"url":"\/documentation\/collectorencoding","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","title":"CollectorEncoding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write batches of records in TraffluentCollector’s ingest format, for an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" to send."}],"role":"collection"},"doc://AsyncQueues/documentation/AsyncQueues":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues","title":"AsyncQueues","url":"\/documentation\/asyncqueues","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The sequence type of every report and delivery stream the library hands out, read by one task at a time."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"type":"topic","title":"Automatic Tracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen."}]},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting":{"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting","title":"DestinationTesting","abstract":[{"text":"Check from Swift Testing that a vendor destination keeps the library’s rules and sends what its fixtures record.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/GettingStarted":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/GettingStarted","title":"Getting Started","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/gettingstarted","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Traffluent to an app, declare its events, deliver them to a server and test what the app tracks."}]},"doc://AutomaticControlTracking/documentation/AutomaticControlTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/automaticcontroltracking","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","type":"topic","title":"AutomaticControlTracking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track a control activation each time a touch activates a UIKit control, without a call on each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"control."}],"role":"collection"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"type":"topic","title":"HTTPDestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PrivacyManifests":{"type":"topic","title":"Privacy Manifests","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels."}]},"doc://Events/documentation/Events":{"url":"\/documentation\/events","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","title":"Events","abstract":[{"text":"The types every other module shares: the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"text":" protocol, the values its properties can hold, and the record a tracker makes of each event.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection"},"doc://TrackingPlanTesting/documentation/TrackingPlanTesting":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","title":"TrackingPlanTesting","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplantesting","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fail a Swift Testing test when an app’s events no longer match its committed tracking plan, so every change to an event comes with a change to the plan."}]},"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers":{"url":"\/documentation\/trackers","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","title":"Trackers","abstract":[{"text":"The tracker app code tracks events with, and what it applies to each event before it is delivered: enrichers, samplers and consent.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection"},"doc://PropertyJSON/documentation/PropertyJSON":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON","title":"PropertyJSON","url":"\/documentation\/propertyjson","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The vendor-neutral pieces a JSON "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" is built from: properties, context, timestamps, identity and batch splitting."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingFromViews":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","title":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give views the tracker the way each framework passes values down, and let modifiers and controls track what views do."}],"role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tell the people and services that read your events what each event holds, and hear about a change that would break their data before it ships."}],"role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","type":"topic","title":"Sampling Events","abstract":[{"text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","title":"Sessions and Standard Context","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/IdentifyingPeople":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","title":"Identifying People","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/identifyingpeople","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Traffluent knows people only by a pseudonymous session. An identifier that outlives one is yours to add, store, reset and gate with consent.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Checksums/documentation/Checksums":{"url":"\/documentation\/checksums","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums","title":"Checksums","abstract":[{"text":"The CRC-32 checksum of raw bytes, as zlib, PNG, gzip and Ethernet compute it.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/WritingAVendorDestination":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WritingAVendorDestination","title":"Writing a Vendor Destination","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/writingavendordestination","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Send events to an analytics vendor Traffluent doesn’t cover yet, from a module of your own, with the same rules as the destinations it ships.","type":"text"}]},"doc://LifecycleTracking/documentation/LifecycleTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/lifecycletracking","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","type":"topic","title":"LifecycleTracking","abstract":[{"text":"Track the app’s installs, updates, opens, moves to the background and terminations, and make the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker’s records durable as the app leaves the foreground.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection"},"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","title":"EventMacros","u